Here is the Java code to implement this program:

```java
import java.util.Random;
import java.util.Scanner;

public class PalindromeGenerator {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter the length of the palindrome: ");
        int length = scanner.nextInt();

        Random random = new Random();
        String randomString = "";
        for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {
            randomString += (char) ('a' + random.nextInt(26));
        }

        String reversedString = new StringBuilder(randomString).reverse().toString();

        while (!randomString.equals(reversedString)) {
            randomString = "";
            for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {
                randomString += (char) ('a' + random.nextInt(26));
            }
            reversedString = new StringBuilder(randomString).reverse().toString();
        }

        System.out.println("The generated palindrome is: " + reversedString);
    }
}
```

